380: with the normal Pontryagin clutching number, and gives
381: \[
382:                     \langle p_1(\bar\nu),[\bar X]\rangle=0.
383:  \tag{K30.20}
384: \]
385: This retains the full normal bundle and all lower-degree
386: frame data; it does not assert that the bundle is trivial.
387: 
388: ## 5. The individual integers and the relative coordinates
389: 
390: The already proved actual page-line comparison gives
391: \[
392:  b^2=4c_1(N)^2=-4H,\qquad
393:  p_1(T\bar X)=-24\chi .
394:  \tag{K30.21}
395: \]
396: The signed trace bordism has positive meridian integral
397: for each norm sign. Its sphere-bundle characteristic
398: formulas, in the matched normal framing just constructed,
399: are
400: \[
401:  k=\frac{p_1(\bar\nu)+3b^2}{4},\qquad
402:  \ell=p_1(T\bar X)+p_1(\bar\nu).
403:  \tag{K30.22}
404: \]
405: Substitution of (K30.20)--(K30.21) proves
406: \(k=-3H\), \(\ell=-24\chi\).
407: The actual line and height equality
408: \(H=2\chi+2(P\cdot O)\) makes both integers integral.
409: The full K23 coordinate morphism is
410: \[
411:  m_{\rm rel}=-k+6A=-\ell/4,\qquad
412:  n_{\rm rel}=-6A,\qquad s=A\bmod28 .
413:  \tag{K30.23}
414: \]
415: Together with the independently proved
416: \(A=\chi-H/2\), this gives (K30.1).
417: 
418: The construction fixes the initial Cox quaternion product,
419: the signed cusp product, and its actual transport. The
420: possible constant rotation loop extends over the fixed
421: three-disc and changes neither number. The formula is for
422: one positive loop in the stated \(r\) parameter; it has not
423: been divided by the page degree, by a source-root order,
424: or by the number of scalar turns in \(\lambda\).
425: 
426: ## Certificate
427: 
428: The exact source-phase and normal-matrix identities are
429: executed in code/part3/general_cap_framing.py. It also
430: combines the already certified K26 and K28 page arithmetic
431: with (K30.22)--(K30.23). The actual normal comparison is
432: the explicit map and clutch proof above.
